    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Define the functions $$\\begin{aligned}f(x)&=2^x+2^{-x}\\\\g(x)&=2^x-2^{-x}.\\end{aligned}$$ Show that $$(f(x))^2-(g(x))^2=4.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(f(x))^2-(g(x))^2=4$.\n\nUse the difference of two squares and $2^x2^{-x}=1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(f(x))^2-(g(x))^2&=(f(x)-g(x))(f(x)+g(x))\\\\(f(x))^2-(g(x))^2&=(2\\cdot2^{-x})(2\\cdot2^x)\\\\(f(x))^2-(g(x))^2&=4\\cdot2^{-x+x}\\\\(f(x))^2-(g(x))^2&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
